================================================================================
CS744 Lab 4 - Load Test 3: Square Calculation (Lightweight compute)
================================================================================

1. AIM:
   How do thread pools and concurrency affect throughput and latency for quick arithmetic operations?

2. SETUP & EXECUTION:
   Machine: Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11400H @ 2.70GHz (6 physical cores, 12 hyperthreads)
   Server core assignment: taskset -c 0,1 (Physical Cores 0 and 1)
   Load generator (wrk) assignment: taskset -c 2,3,4,5 (Physical Cores 2, 3, 4, 5)
   Measurement duration: 10s per point
   Varying parameter: Concurrency -c over [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128]
   Client threads: -t = min(c, 4)
   Metrics: Throughput (requests/sec) and Mean Response Time (ms)

3. HYPOTHESIS:
   Performance will sit between the CPU-heavy prime test and the pure I/O test. Adding workers up to the core count (2 workers) will scale throughput close to 2x single-threaded. Concurrency increases beyond saturation will lead to linearly rising response times in accordance with Little's Law.

